From eec6ff94bf0619230dc4ae5b05eb8874ddba0fef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:03:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] es_out: take no clock reference as late while the input is
 paused

A paused input demuxes on demand while a decoder still owes the picture
a paused seek or a frame step asks for. Its clock stands still, but each
clock reference reached meanwhile was compared with the wall clock, and
once the decoder took long enough, as MediaCodec's MPEG-4 Part 2 decoder
does after a video track is selected again, it was taken as late: the
input reset the clock, flushing the decoders, and the paused picture was
lost along with the key picture it was decoded from.

As while stepping frames, take no reference as late while paused.
---
 src/input/es_out.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/input/es_out.c b/src/input/es_out.c
index ed4f970..1295bf9 100644
--- a/src/input/es_out.c
+++ b/src/input/es_out.c
@@ -2539,6 +2539,12 @@ static int EsOutControlLocked( es_out_t *out, int i_query, va_list args )
             if( p_sys->p_next_frame_es != NULL )
                 return VLC_SUCCESS;
 
+            /* Paused, the clock stands still: the input demuxes only for a
+             * decoder that still owes its picture, and a clock reference it
+             * reaches meanwhile cannot be late. */
+            if( p_sys->b_paused )
+                return VLC_SUCCESS;
+
             if( b_late && ( !input_priv(p_sys->p_input)->p_sout ||
                             !input_priv(p_sys->p_input)->b_out_pace_control ) )
             {
